From: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas571x: add TAS5751M and PurePath Console register scripts

The TAS5751M has the TAS5733/TAS5753 register layout (2-byte volumes,
the same biquad, cross-over biquad and output mixer addresses) with its
own reset defaults (TI SLASEC1B, 7.7.1). Add it with:

- PVDD sequenced after AVDD/DVDD and after RST/PDN have been released,
  as the start-up sequence in the data sheet (8.2.1.2.5.1) asks for, and
  the matching power-down sequence (8.2.1.2.5.4) on remove and on probe
  failure: shutdown, soft-stop wait, PDN/RST, PVDD off, a decay wait,
  only then AVDD/DVDD;
- a guard against sending exit-shutdown during the first 240 ms + 1.3 *
  tstart after the oscillator trim, which the chip silently ignores. It
  is kept in ktime and only armed for chips that need it, so the other
  parts see no change;
- an optional "firmware-name" register script in the PurePath Console
  text format, loaded right after the trim. Boards such as the Yandex
  Station ship their complete amplifier tuning (EQ, DRC, PBTL output mux,
  mixers) only in this form.

Signed-off-by: MyszkinPL <211237936+MyszkinPL@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas57xx.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/ti,tas57xx.yaml
index 0b013a3..cad4611 100644
